  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the Issue Tracker's seven-scale composite grader. gradeIssue(data) grades each of priority/severity/magnitude/harm/failure-condition/MoSCoW/frequency independently and takes compositePriority as the worst (max) band across all seven; a NULL score bands as 'low' for that instrument but pushes NO rule at all (not even a low one) - only a non-null score produces a R-<INSTRUMENT>-<value> rule - so firedRules.length varies with how many of the 7 scores are answered, plus one trailing R-COMPOSITE-<BAND> rule that is always present. additionalFlags are independent threshold checks on the raw scores (not the bands) and fire regardless of the composite: harm===4 (not merely >=4, since 4 is the harm scale's maximum), failure==='A', severity===5, magnitude===10, frequency>=95, moscow===1, and (issueCategory in the regulatory set) AND harm>=2 together. Regenerate 'expected' with: bin/test-personas issue-tracker --update",
